IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgg-scope`
IMPORT `sgg-identity`

-- Tests for sgg-identity.l4 (ss 375 and 376). Expected values are written from the text of each subsection, beside the assertion.
-- Dates: Date day month year. A `-- EXPECT` comment above a #TRACE says what the trace must print; the lead checks each against the output.

§ `Section 375(1)(b): the name and the place of formation on its documents`

-- Arguments: the document is one of the listed documents; the name and the place are stated on it in legible romanised letters.
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(b) the document states the name and the place of formation in legible romanised letters` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(b) the document states the name and the place of formation in legible romanised letters` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a document that is not a bill-head, letter paper, notice, prospectus or other official publication is outside the duty: the text says nothing about it.
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(b) the document states the name and the place of formation in legible romanised letters` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(b) the document states the name and the place of formation in legible romanised letters` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- no deadline in the text: with no event the duty stays open, and an act at any time fulfils it.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 375(1)(b) the foreign company must cause its name and place of formation to be stated in legible romanised letters` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 375(1)(b) the foreign company must cause its name and place of formation to be stated in legible romanised letters` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 375(1)(b) cause its name and the place where it is formed or incorporated to be stated in legible romanised letters` AT 400

§ `Section 375(1)(c): notice that the liability of the members is limited`

-- Arguments: the liability of its members is limited; the last word of the name.
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(c) the foreign company must cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given` TRUE "Pte" EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "unless the last word of its name is the word Limited or Berhad or the abbreviation Ltd. or Bhd.": each of the four ends the duty.
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(c) the foreign company must cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given` TRUE "Limited" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(c) the foreign company must cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given` TRUE "Berhad" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(c) the foreign company must cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given` TRUE "Ltd." EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(c) the foreign company must cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given` TRUE "Bhd." EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "if the liability of its members is limited": when it is not, the duty does not arise.
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(c) the foreign company must cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given` FALSE "Pte" EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(c) the foreign company must cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given` FALSE "Limited" EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the text names the abbreviation with its full stop; "Ltd" without one is not in the list (marginal reading, NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(c) the foreign company must cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given` TRUE "Ltd" EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- (i) in every prospectus issued by it and in all its bill-heads, letter paper, notices and other official publications in Singapore.
-- Arguments: the document is one of those; the notice is stated on it in legible characters.
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(c)(i) the document states notice that the liability of the members is limited in legible characters` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(c)(i) the document states notice that the liability of the members is limited in legible characters` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(c)(i) the document states notice that the liability of the members is limited in legible characters` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (ii) "except in the case of a banking corporation": a banking corporation need not exhibit the notice outside its premises.
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(c)(ii) the foreign company must exhibit the notice outside its registered office and every place of business it has established in Singapore` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 375(1)(c)(ii) the foreign company must exhibit the notice outside its registered office and every place of business it has established in Singapore` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- no deadline in the text.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 375(1)(c) the foreign company must cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 375(1)(c) the foreign company must cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 375(1)(c) cause notice that the liability of its members is limited to be given` AT 400

§ `Section 375(2): a name shown otherwise than in romanised letters`

-- Arguments: the name is indicated in characters or in another way than romanised letters; the name is also stated in romanised letters not smaller than any of the characters.
#ASSERT `s 375(2) the section relating to the statement of the name is deemed not to have been complied with` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "unless the name of the company is stated on such document in romanised letters not smaller than any of the characters": once it is, the deeming does not apply, and the subsection does not say the section is complied with.
#ASSERT `s 375(2) the section relating to the statement of the name is deemed not to have been complied with` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "Where the name ... is indicated ... in characters": when it is not, the subsection does not speak.
#ASSERT `s 375(2) the section relating to the statement of the name is deemed not to have been complied with` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 375(2) the section relating to the statement of the name is deemed not to have been complied with` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 375(3): the unique entity number`

-- Arguments: the document is a business letter, statement of account, invoice, official notice or publication of the company; the number issued by the Registrar appears on it in a legible form.
#ASSERT `s 375(3) the document shows the unique entity number in a legible form` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 375(3) the document shows the unique entity number in a legible form` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 375(3) the document shows the unique entity number in a legible form` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- no deadline in the text.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 375(3) the foreign company must cause its unique entity number to appear in a legible form on its business letters and other documents` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 375(3) the foreign company must cause its unique entity number to appear in a legible form on its business letters and other documents` "Overseas Co" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 365 the foreign company` "Overseas Co" DOES `s 375(3) cause its unique entity number to appear in a legible form` AT 400

§ `Section 375(4): a foreign company incorporated before 3 January 2016`

-- Arguments: incorporated before 3 January 2016; the day asked.
-- "after the expiration of 12 months after that date": 3 January 2016 + 12 months expires with 3 January 2017, so subsection (3) bites from 4 January 2017.
#ASSERT `s 375(4) the foreign company must comply with subsection (3) on the day asked` TRUE (Date 3 1 2017) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 375(4) the foreign company must comply with subsection (3) on the day asked` TRUE (Date 4 1 2017) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 375(4) the foreign company must comply with subsection (3) on the day asked` TRUE (Date 2 1 2016) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 375(4) the foreign company must comply with subsection (3) on the day asked` TRUE (Date 1 6 2016) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 375(4) the foreign company must comply with subsection (3) on the day asked` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a company incorporated on or after 3 January 2016 is not the company the relief names: the text says nothing for it.
#ASSERT `s 375(4) the foreign company must comply with subsection (3) on the day asked` FALSE (Date 1 6 2016) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 376: service of a document on a foreign company`

-- Arguments: the document is required to be served on the foreign company; (a) addressed to the company and left at, or posted to, its registered office in Singapore;
-- (b) addressed to an authorised representative and left at, or posted to, the representative's residential address or contact address;
-- the company has ceased to maintain a place of business in Singapore; (c) addressed to the company and left at, or posted to, its registered office in the place of its incorporation.
#ASSERT `s 376 the document is sufficiently served on the foreign company` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 376 the document is sufficiently served on the foreign company` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 376 the document is sufficiently served on the foreign company` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c): ceased, and addressed to the home registered office
-- (c) is for a company that has ceased to maintain a place of business in Singapore: a company that has not ceased is not served by posting to its home registered office.
#ASSERT `s 376 the document is sufficiently served on the foreign company` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a company that has ceased, but the document went nowhere the section names.
#ASSERT `s 376 the document is sufficiently served on the foreign company` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 376 the document is sufficiently served on the foreign company` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a document not required to be served on the foreign company is not one the section speaks to.
#ASSERT `s 376 the document is sufficiently served on the foreign company` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
